    Question: Philip has a farm with animals. He has 20 cows, 50% more ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. How many animals does Philip have on his farm? Think step by step. Answer:If Philip has 20 cows, he has 20 * 50% = 10 more ducks than cows, so he has 20 + 10 = 30 ducks. Philip has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total, so he has 30 * 1/5 = 6 pigs. Therefore, Philip has a total of 20 cows + 30 ducks + 6 pigs = 56 animals on his farm. #### 56 The answer is: 56

